    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d683">

                <pb facs="0803" n="793" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg793"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.3516/9–2948: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kohler</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-09-29T19:00:00+03:00">September 29,
                            1948—7 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 30—12:50 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2187. Am following up with Foreign Office without result so far question Dairen
                    telegrams, none which yet received here (Embtel 2057 to Department September 20,
                    repeated Nanking 27, Shanghai 30, Dairen 18).</p>
                <p>Sent Department 2187. Department pass Nanking 33, Shanghai 31, Dairen 19.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kohler</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
